# What Debian calls the things profiles ask for.
#
# Many of these are genuine Debian virtual packages, in which case the
# alias is redundant and harmless: expansion keeps the original name
# first, so the real capability wins.

Capability: web-browser
Resolves-To: firefox | firefox-esr | chromium | epiphany-browser

Capability: terminal-emulator
Resolves-To: foot | alacritty | kitty | wezterm | x-terminal-emulator | konsole | gnome-terminal | xterm | qterminal

Capability: file-manager
Resolves-To: dolphin | nautilus | thunar | pcmanfm | pcmanfm-qt

Capability: text-editor
Resolves-To: editor | kate | gedit | nano | featherpad

Capability: document-viewer
Resolves-To: evince | okular | atril | qpdfview

Capability: image-viewer
Resolves-To: eog | gwenview | ristretto | lximage-qt

Capability: word-processor
Resolves-To: libreoffice-writer | abiword

Capability: spreadsheet
Resolves-To: libreoffice-calc | gnumeric

Capability: mail-transport-agent
Resolves-To: postfix | exim4-daemon-light | nullmailer | msmtp-mta

Capability: audio-server
Resolves-To: pipewire | pulseaudio

Capability: vulkan-driver
Resolves-To: mesa-vulkan-drivers | nvidia-driver-libs

Capability: opengl
Resolves-To: libgl1 | libgl1-mesa-glx

Capability: firewall
Resolves-To: ufw | nftables | iptables

Capability: time-sync
Resolves-To: systemd-timesyncd | chrony | ntp

Capability: ssh-server
Resolves-To: openssh-server

Capability: compiler-toolchain
Resolves-To: build-essential | gcc

Capability: vpn-client
Resolves-To: wireguard-tools

Capability: steam
Resolves-To: steam-installer | steam

Capability: init
Resolves-To: systemd-sysv | sysvinit-core | runit-init

Capability: c-library
Resolves-To: libc6 | libc6.1 | musl

Capability: core-utilities
Resolves-To: coreutils

Capability: package-manager
Resolves-To: apt

Capability: archiver
Resolves-To: tar

Capability: desktop-session
Resolves-To: plasma-desktop | gnome-shell | xfce4-session | lxqt-wayland-session

Capability: display-manager
Resolves-To: sddm | gdm3 | lightdm

Capability: archive-manager
Resolves-To: ark | file-roller | xarchiver | lxqt-archiver

Capability: system-settings
Resolves-To: systemsettings | gnome-control-center | lxqt-config

# gnome-shell is last on purpose. Since GNOME 42 the screenshot
# tool is part of the shell rather than a package of its own, so
# a machine can have the capability with nothing named after it
# installed. Aliases go stale this way: ecosystems absorb tools
# into larger packages, and the alias still names the tool.
Capability: screenshot-tool
Resolves-To: kde-spectacle | spectacle | flameshot | gnome-screenshot | xfce4-screenshooter | gnome-shell | screengrab

Capability: lightweight-session
Resolves-To: openbox | i3-wm | fluxbox | xfce4-session

Capability: compositor-effects
Resolves-To: kwin-wayland | kwin-x11 | mutter | compiz

Capability: icon-theme
Resolves-To: breeze-icon-theme | adwaita-icon-theme | papirus-icon-theme

Capability: cursor-theme
Resolves-To: breeze-cursor-theme | adwaita-icon-theme

Capability: font-collection
Resolves-To: fonts-noto | fonts-dejavu | fonts-liberation

Capability: network-applet
Resolves-To: plasma-nm | network-manager-gnome | nm-tray

Capability: volume-applet
Resolves-To: plasma-pa | pavucontrol | pasystray | pavucontrol-qt

Capability: desktop-portal
Resolves-To: xdg-desktop-portal-kde | xdg-desktop-portal-gnome | xdg-desktop-portal-gtk | xdg-desktop-portal-lxqt

Capability: window-manager
Resolves-To: sway | hyprland | i3-wm | bspwm | dwm | river | labwc

Capability: status-bar
Resolves-To: waybar | polybar | i3status | lemonbar

Capability: application-launcher
Resolves-To: fuzzel | rofi | wofi | dmenu | bemenu | lxqt-runner

Capability: notification-daemon
Resolves-To: mako-notifier | dunst | notification-daemon | lxqt-notificationd

Capability: screen-locker
Resolves-To: swaylock | i3lock | xsecurelock | slock

Capability: wallpaper-setter
Resolves-To: swaybg | feh | nitrogen | hsetroot

Capability: compositor
Resolves-To: picom | compton | xcompmgr

Capability: modern-shell
Resolves-To: zsh | fish

Capability: terminal-multiplexer
Resolves-To: tmux | zellij | screen

Capability: fuzzy-finder
Resolves-To: fzf | skim

Capability: network-scanner
Resolves-To: nmap | masscan | zmap

Capability: packet-analyser
Resolves-To: wireshark | tshark | tcpdump | termshark

Capability: password-cracker
Resolves-To: john | hashcat | hydra

Capability: web-scanner
Resolves-To: nikto | dirb | gobuster | wapiti

Capability: network-auditor
Resolves-To: aircrack-ng | kismet | bettercap

Capability: reverse-engineering
Resolves-To: radare2 | rizin | ghidra | gdb

Capability: forensics-toolkit
Resolves-To: sleuthkit | binwalk | foremost | testdisk

Capability: exploitation-framework
Resolves-To: metasploit-framework

Capability: network-manager
Resolves-To: network-manager | connman | systemd-networkd

Capability: network-manager-wifi
Resolves-To: network-manager

Capability: wifi-supplicant
Resolves-To: wpasupplicant | iwd

# The add-ons of 26 September: media, school and vpn.

Capability: music-player
Resolves-To: elisa | rhythmbox

# Debian's Firefox decodes H.264 through ffmpeg; the extra build
# carries the codecs the default one leaves out.
Capability: browser-h264
Resolves-To: libavcodec-extra

Capability: presentation
Resolves-To: libreoffice-impress

Capability: mail-client
Resolves-To: thunderbird | evolution

Capability: pdf-annotator
Resolves-To: xournalpp

Capability: typing-tutor
Resolves-To: ktouch

Capability: spell-check-english
Resolves-To: hunspell-en-us

Capability: openvpn-client
Resolves-To: network-manager-openvpn

